      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al0.2Co1.5CrFeNi1.5Ti0.3 is a high-entropy alloy.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The additively manufactured alloy contains two populations of nanoprecipitates dispersed in a homogeneous matrix.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The nanoprecipitates are enriched in Ti and Cr.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ti- and Cr-rich nanoprecipitates act as local elemental reservoirs during oxidation.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "In-situ APT can track oxidation-induced elemental redistribution in real time under high-temperature oxidizing conditions.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Under oxidation conditions, Ti preferentially segregates from nanoprecipitates to the alloy/oxide interface.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Under oxidation conditions, Cr preferentially segregates from nanoprecipitates to the alloy/oxide interface.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Accumulation of Ti and Cr at the alloy/oxide interface nucleates a dense protective oxide layer.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The dense protective oxide layer slows further oxidation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "APT will reveal measurable elemental gradients at nanoprecipitate interfaces.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ti and Cr accumulation will coincide with early-stage protective oxide formation.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed redistribution and oxide formation will correlate with better oxidation resistance than in cast and wrought forms of the same alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "APT is well suited to characterize atomic-scale elemental redistribution.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Changes in oxidation atmosphere or alloy-processing parameters may produce different elemental-redistribution behavior.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
